<title>CHINA: China's Xinjiang stuck with unsold grain - paper.</title>
<headline>China's Xinjiang stuck with unsold grain - paper.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers in China's northwestern region of Xinjiang are unable to sell large amounts of grain due to problems with storing last year's bumper harvest, the People's Daily Overseas Edition said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Although state purchasing targets for 1996 had been met, local farmers still had much unsold grain, including 400,000 tonnes of maize, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Local authorities had been buying corn at the state price of 1,060 yuan ($121) per tonne since the end of February and had purchased nearly 150,000 tonnes by April 15, it said.</p>
<p>Grain output in Xinjiang hit 7.8 million tonnes last year, of which maize production rose by 339,000 tonnes to 3.09 million tonnes, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
